        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Craig Nicholls, Boy George, David Byrne, Josh Groban, Steven Page, Rufus Wainwright\n- Organizations: The Vines\n- Works: “Get Free”, If I Loved You: Gentlemen Prefer Broadway\n- Roles: singer, songwriter, guitarist, DJ, fashion designer, photographer\n\nFacts:\n- Boy George was born as George Alan O'Dowd on 14 June 1961.\n- Boy George is an English singer, songwriter, DJ, fashion designer, and photographer.\n- Craig Robert Nicholls was born on 31 August 1977.\n- Craig Nicholls is an Australian musician best known as the lead singer, songwriter, and guitarist of the Australian alternative rock band The Vines.\n- Craig Nicholls is the only mainstay member of The Vines.\n- The song “Get Free” was written by The Vines frontman Craig Nicholls.\n- The concert If I Loved You: Gentlemen Prefer Broadway featured men singing classic love songs to one another.\n- If I Loved You: Gentlemen Prefer Broadway included a full orchestra and performances by Rufus Wainwright and special guests Boy George, David Byrne, Josh Groban, and Steven Page.",
